{
  "decision": "PROPOSE",
  "rationale": "The requirement asks for client access to server network 10.0.2.0/24 to be allowed and access to management network 10.0.99.0/24 to be blocked on r1. This aligns with the declared access policy: client-to-server access is permitted, and client-to-management access is denied. The routing requirement is actionable: r1 must be configured to route traffic to 10.0.2.0/24 via r2 through the transit network 10.0.12.0/30, using next hop 10.0.12.2 (r2's interface). The access policy rule for blocking client-to-management access on r1 is explicitly required and valid. No unsafe operations or invalid inventory are involved. Static routes are feasible and within policy.",
